+// The split kernel for T <= 8 rows: a work-group a (key head, split) for all rows, the split's keys and values (the union
+// of the rows' ranges) in local memory once. Each (row, query head) takes P sub-groups: sub-group u of them computes the
+// logits of keys lane + 16 v for v in [u 4/P, (u+1) 4/P) and the value sums of dims [u D/P, (u+1) D/P). Every value is
+// the one the one-row kernel below computes: the same lane a key (counted from the row's own first key) and so the same
+// dimension rotation, the same fma chains in the same order, the maximum over all the split's keys (exact in any order),
+// the probabilities' sum as each lane's 4 in key-slice order and then the same sub-group sum, each dim's value sum over
+// the keys in order. Only the tile is shared and the work spread (ideas: steveseguin b70-optimization-lab inkling2, check
+// steps reading each key once for all their tokens; small kernels with the reads issued first).
